WEBVTT

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.650
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:37.490
Please do not glower so severely 
at my precious fiancée.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.080
F-Fiancée?

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.750
You belong to me.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.550
Isn't that right?

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.360
Huh?

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.230
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.670
My precious fiancée.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.690
You belong to me.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.100
Isn't that right?

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.660
W-Wha? Eh?

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.390
What are you trying to pull?

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.660
Mori Ougai-dono.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:51.300
<i>Mori Ougai?</i>

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.390
Why, if it isn't the 
young lady from earlier!

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.070
I was rather curious about this earlier,

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.910
but this design is quite reasonable, 
yet innovative and revolutionary.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.700
I knew you would understand, Koizumi-san.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:14.460
Yes, that's right, what she 
is wearing is a short...

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.960
...skirt!...

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.130
...that is all the rage in the West right now.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.870
Yes! It's a skirt.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.450
Oh, a skart.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.080
No, skirt!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.610
Yes, a skirt!

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:30.760
Huh?

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:39.610
If we linger here any longer, that scary 
police officer might come after us.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.750
You don't have anywhere 
to go tonight, do you?

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.750
My mansion has many available rooms, 
if you would like.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.000
Hang on, Ougai-san.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.260
It wasn't a dream...?

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.770
<b>Sukiyaki Is Romance Veiled in Steam</b>

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.420
In other words, you traveled back in time.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.540
Time travel?!

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:41.940
I traveled back in time?

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.430
<b>Boom</b>

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.680
We're being attacked!

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:55.930
This is precisely why I told him I 
didn't want her room next to mine.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.540
W-W-We're being attacked by bad guys!

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:00.050
What're you talking about?

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.580
That, that...!

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.820
That's just the midday cannon.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.940
<b>Midday 
Cannon</b>

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.160
T-The cannon?

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.180
It fires blanks to inform 
us when it is midday.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:08.230
You've even forgotten about that?

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:12.200
Anyway, could you maybe 
do something about <i>that</i>?

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.220
Th-These are...

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.390
They're so beautiful!

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.340
Hey...

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.110
Huh?

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.910
You haven't finished this one yet?

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.220
There's nothing in the middle.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.820
<i>I guess I shouldn't have asked about it...</i>

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.990
There you are, Little Squirrel.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.840
Oh, when did you get back?

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.770
I got back just now, Fumi-san.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.110
I heard the Little Squirrel's 
voice from the second floor.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.860
U-Umm... Who is this Little Squirrel?

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.880
That would be you.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:07.700
It is what came to mind when we 
first met and I saw you trembling.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.150
Ah, I see.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.260
Have you remembered anything, 
Little Squirrel?

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:17.640
About your home or your parents?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.790
Uh, no, nothing yet.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.750
You traveled back in time.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:30.030
<i>I probably shouldn't tell him that. 
There's no way he'd believe me.</i>

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.240
I thought you might remember 
something after a night of rest,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.040
but I guess it will not be so easy.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.180
Well, let's give it some time.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:43.480
You are welcome to stay here 
until your memory returns.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:45.190
Can I?

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:47.170
Of course. Right, Syunso?

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.220
I don't have any objections.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.080
Especially since I'm just a freeloader, too.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.940
Thank you so much!

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:57.430
I will do my best to remember things so
I can leave as soon as possible.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.220
<i>I have to hurry up and 
get back to my own time.</i>

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:06.960
You are welcome to stay forever, 
even if your memories return.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:14.640
After all, you are my fiancée.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:16.820
Isn't that right?

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.040
Now then, why don't we get something to eat?

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.450
It will be a welcome party 
for you, Little Squirrel.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.330
What would you like to eat?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:32.000
No way, just letting me stay 
here is more than enough!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.630
You don't need to go through 
such trouble for me...

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.350
<b>Growl</b>

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:39.610
Well, I guess a small beef 
bowl would be nice...

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:45.610
<b>Beef 
Bowl</b>

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.100
Beef bowl?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.230
Are you referring to sukiyaki?

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.590
That's a pretty audacious request.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:49.210
No, no, it doesn't need to 
be anything so expensive.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:52.100
Just one of the 380 yen bowls.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:54.370
380 yen?!

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.370
<b>380 Yen</b>

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.570
Do you want to buy out 
the place or something?

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:02.090
Perhaps you are the daughter of an 
extremely rich family, Little Squirrel?

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:03.620
Huh? Eh? Wha?

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:07.500
I-I see now. The value of money 
is different in this time,

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.710
so I gotta be careful.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:13.160
Umm, so how do I wear this stuff?

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:33.140
E-Excuse me!

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.510
Yes?

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:38.690
It must be hard work, cleaning 
this big mansion all by yourself.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.030
Yes, it really is.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:45.550
<i>They don't have vacuum cleaners 
or mops in this time yet, either.</i>

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.780
Oh my.

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:58.430
That looks rather nice on you.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.800
You're finally dressed appropriately.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.010
I managed somehow, thanks to Fumi-san's help.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:08.550
She's even forgotten how to wear a kimono.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.320
<i>A Meiji era city...</i>

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.560
<i>Mori Ougai-san...</i>

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:26.870
<i>He's </i>the<i> Mori Ougai-san!</i>

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.670
<b>Sukiyaki</b>

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.680
<b>Iroha 
Sukiyaki</b>

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.660
Now, help yourself.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.310
If it's not enough, we can 
order as much as you'd like.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.560
O-Okay! Thank you for the food.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:15.840
It's so good!

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:19.440
You really like beef.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.930
Yes!

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.700
So you can still remember what you like,
 even with the amnesia.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.070
Yes, yes.

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:29.090
It just melts on my tongue.

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:31.970
This is the taste of high-quality protein.

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:38.480
Syunso, this reminds me 
of the day we met.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.260
It was a year ago.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:53.660
Eat beef from a pot,
and your tongue will burn.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.500
That doesn't quite work, sir.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:59.560
Two out, bases loaded, huh?

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.050
One 
Year 
Ago

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:32.960
How magnificent!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.560
I've never seen such a 
beautiful creature before.

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:37.690
May I pet you?

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.710
The shiny luster of your black coat...

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:46.220
A supple body that is elegantly streamlined,

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:50.610
and bewitching golden eyes 
that seduce the beholder.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:56.090
You're like an artwork of ultimate 
natural beauty made by the divine!

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:06.860
P-Pervert!

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.230
And that's how the two of you met?

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:17.540
Indeed, Little Squirrel. It was quite 
a stimulating encounter, wouldn't you say?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.000
That's not how I remember it!

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.590
Syunso gets so taken with artistic passion

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:26.720
when he finds a wonderful model 
that he loses himself.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.850
How troublesome.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.000
You're the one who's troublesome!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.640
Could you please stop getting naked 
all the time at 6 o'clock?!

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:34.930
I can't do that.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.310
I am the kind of person who isn't satisfied

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.030
unless my schedule is carried out regularly.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:44.430
My schedule is such that I bathe each day,
 morning and evening, at 6 o'clock.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:51.620
So that's how the two of 
you began living together?

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:52.650
Yes.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.790
When I looked at the drawing Syunso had made,

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:59.000
I thought that this man would surely one day

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.840
carry the weight of Japan's 
art world on his shoulders.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:05.590
I decided to have him come stay in my 
mansion since I found him fascinating.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.000
Because he's fascinating?

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.540
Yes, because he's fascinating.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:13.950
By the way, Little Squirrel, 
may I ask you something?

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.180
Sure.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.430
Do you like cats?

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:20.770
Cats?

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:24.440
Yes, I'm decently fond of them.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:29.220
Wonderful. Then, would you mind 
finding Syunso's black cat?

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.200
You had a black cat as a pet, Syunso-san?

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.200
Yes, I guess you could say it was a pet.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.000
Ougai-san.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.530
What's the harm?

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.720
Besides, your exhibition is coming up soon,

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.510
and it is about time you were 
recognized by the art world.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:48.900
I fully understand!

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:51.060
I would be more than happy to help.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.660
Should I make up some posters?

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:56.230
Missing

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:56.220
That's a good idea. 
Posters could be rather effective.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:14:01.480
But your powers as a Tamayori will 
be needed to find Syunso's cat.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.850
Eh? Tamayori?

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:11.000
That's if you are truly a Tamayori, though.

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:12.790
Umm...

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.500
What is a Tamayori?

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:16.500
Fling

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:22.250
Ah, yes, you do have amnesia.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:26.010
It is a name generally given to those who can

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.890
see things not of this world. 
Spirits, in other words.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.260
Spirits and those who could see them,

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.770
the Tamayori, were not uncommon 
in Japan in the past.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:41.920
However, with the progression of 
modernization since the Meiji Restoration,

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:44.200
a great number of the 
spirits went into hiding,

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:48.530
and the Tamayori's numbers 
continued to decrease.

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:52.660
Tamayori are now incredibly valuable.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.660
Are you a Tamayori?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.130
Tamayori...

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:01.670
Yes. Our conversation has 
carried on a bit long,

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.460
so why don't we get to eating this meat?

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:06.180
Okay.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:12.420
A black cat?

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.700
That's what was missing from the painting.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:17.970
A black cat!

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.930
That's right. You figured it out quickly.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:27.680
<i>But how did I know that?</i>

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:32.500
Sometimes such things happen to 
creative works full of soul.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.200
It is the sign of a masterpiece.

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.950
That's why I would like you to find it.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:42.620
It is important to Syunso.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:51.130
That is, if you are indeed a Tamayori.

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:56.050
I did wonder at that time 
if you indeed saw a spirit.

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.390
That time...?

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.090
<i>Do I really have such power?</i>

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:18.110
Mei-chan, Mei-chan, Mei-chan!

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:19.980
<i>What?</i>

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:24.280
<i>What is this voice?</i>

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:26.510
<i>I've heard it somewhere before.</i>

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.320
I...

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.880
All right, that's enough.

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:45.640
Well then, sweet buns are a great 
way to finish up a hot pot meal.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:46.850
Please stop!

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.010
Sweet buns?

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:02.580
<i>What am I supposed to do here?</i>

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:07.860
Hey.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.940
Syunso-san.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:20.140
You don't need to worry about 
what Ougai-san said earlier.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:27.290
There's no way a dense girl 
like you is a Tamayori.

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:29.700
D-Dense?

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.520
Mei-chan.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.630
That man!

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.000
Hey there. You made it.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.480
I knew you would be here!

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.510
You're so good, Mei-chan.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:28.870
Please send me back!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.050
Please send me back to my time!

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:37.560
I am defenseless against that cold
 expression mixed with resentment and scorn.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:40.670
You're the one who brought 
me to this time period!

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:42.810
You should be able to send me back.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:46.700
You want to go back to the 
present time that badly?

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:49.810
I can send you back.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:54.770
I just can't do it right away.

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:59.060
I will need to prepare.

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:06.360
I may be an extraordinary magician, 
but transcending time takes a lot of work.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:10.080
I will need the same conditions 
as when I brought you here.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:13.500
Essentially, the probability of success

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.840
is extremely low unless it is 
 the night of a full moon.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.770
The night of a full moon?

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:25.300
Then I can go back in a month?

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:27.860
To my world, modern day Tokyo!

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:30.250
I can guarantee it.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:35.240
Now, until the one month period is up,

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.100
enjoy this time.

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.420
Just be yourself.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:43.370
Be myself?

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:46.420
Tokyo during the Meiji era is great!

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:50.690
Japanese and Western styles blending 
together at the height of Japan's Westernization.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.950
It has a spirit that is full of energy.

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:54.380
Anything goes!

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.050
You don't need to worry about

00:19:57.050 --> 00:20:00.340
what others think about you or hating 
yourself in such a chaotic age.

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:03.900
You can just comfortably 
be yourself here, Mei-chan!

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.050
Be myself?

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:10.340
You mean...

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:13.970
Your powers as a Tamayori will be needed.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.020
Is that it?

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:19.370
What is it?

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.580
<i>Be myself.</i>

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.990
One month... If it's just one month,

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:30.620
I will try to enjoy this time period.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.800
Syunso-san!

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:50.100
Would you say something before you enter?

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:55.580
Wait, Syunso-san, what are you doing?

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:58.870
I am going to find the black cat.

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:01.530
Huh? What's with you all of the sudden?

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:04.610
I think I am a Tamayori.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:07.610
So I believe I can find the black cat.

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:11.730
I want to see your finished painting!

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:23.020
Oh, Ougai-san.

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.890
Do you have any extra cloth or sticks?

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:29.150
They're finished!

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:32.540
What are those?

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:34.010
Cleaning tools.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:40.670
You use it like this!

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:46.600
See, now this should make things 
a little bit easier on Fumi-san.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.900
Little Squirrel, you...

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:59.090
Do you want to try it too, Fumi-san?

00:21:59.090 --> 00:22:00.910
Yes, I would!

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:06.410
Oh, you are right! This is 
so much easier on my back.

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:07.920
Isn't it?

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:13.700
<i>Just who are you?</i>

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:22.660
Good luck searching for 
the black cat, Mei-chan.

00:22:22.660 --> 00:22:27.990
But there might be lots of other 
fun things waiting for you.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.160
I want to apologize to Jane.

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Next Episode Preview

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Caught in the Ghost Hotel

00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:35.890
If her anger is such that 
she wishes to kill me,

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.230
then I want to answer for that.

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:39.840
What are you talking about?!
